# =============================================================================
# frontend/.env.example
# =============================================================================
# Purpose:
#   Template for the frontend's Vite environment variables. Copy this file to
#   `.env` in the frontend/ directory before running `npm run dev`.
#   The .env file is gitignored — never commit real values.
#
# Usage:
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#
# IMPORTANT — Vite env variable naming:
#   Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser bundle.
#   Variables without this prefix are NOT accessible in client-side code.
#
# Variables:
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL
#   The base URL of the FastAPI backend API.
#   In development, Vite proxies /api → http://localhost:8000/api (see vite.config.js),
#   so you can set this to "/api" and let the proxy handle it (no CORS issues).
#   In production, set this to the full URL of the deployed backend:
#     e.g. https://api.skynest.example.com/api
#
# =============================================================================

VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
